# Test conventions

## Tests run offline

Adapter and pipeline tests use committed fixtures under `tests/fixtures/` and
`tests/discourse/fixtures/`. No test may require live network access to pass.

Tests that genuinely need a running service (Postgres, GROBID) are marked and skipped when
the service is unreachable — they never fail the suite on a machine without Docker running.

## Acceptance criteria are the spec

Each task file lists exact commands. Write the tests that make those commands pass, not
tests that merely look thorough. If a task says a command must exit 0 and print a count,
assert on the exit code and the count.

## Invariant tests — do not weaken, skip, or delete

These exist to catch a non-compliant change regardless of which tool wrote it. Three
different agents work in this repo; these tests are the actual enforcement layer, not the
instruction files.

| Test | Asserts |
|---|---|
| `tests/test_no_direct_litellm.py` | Only `llm/gateway.py` imports `litellm` |
| `tests/test_score_separation.py` | No code path performs arithmetic combining `confidence` and `evidence_quality`; `scoring/` imports nothing from `discourse/` |
| `tests/test_channel_separation.py` | `EvidenceSource` and `DiscourseSource` share no base class; no discourse value reaches `claim_score` |
| `tests/test_extraction_schema.py` | Every extraction table rejects a null `tree_node_id` |
| `tests/test_digest.py` | The digest has separate "Evidence" and "Community attention" sections, and no attention figure appears in the evidence section |

If one of these fails, the fix is the source code — never the test.

## Determinism

LLM calls are mocked in unit tests. A test whose result depends on live model output is not
a unit test. Where model behaviour genuinely matters, assert on structure (a node ID was
returned, a stance is one of three values), not on generated prose.

## Commands

```bash
uv run pytest                  # full suite
uv run pytest tests/test_x.py  # single file
uv run ruff check .            # lint
uv run ruff format --check .   # format
```

Both `pytest` and `ruff check` must pass before any PR.
